\cf2 You move south.\par
It is quite pleasant here in this small grove of trees.  The wind is barely noticeable, while the air is warm and carries the fragrance of many flowers growing along  the lush grassy soil.  There is also soft music, sounds that defy definition.\par
\cf1 \par
listen\par
\cf2 The sounds are ethereal, like a warm fire on a long, cold winter's evening.  It is very relaxing. "Do you like my music?" a gentle voice says, as a fairy flies out from her resting place up in one of the trees.  "My warmest welcome, friend.  My name is Gale," she greets with a smile.  \par
\par
\i You hear a voice, more of a whisper.  The words it speaks are indistinguishable, yet there is an eerie familarity to it.\i0 \par
\cf1 \par
ask gale about mansion\par
\cf2 Gale sighs, as her cheerful disposition momentarily fades.  "It would be best if you didn't need to think about that dreadful place...  But I fear it may be your only hope of rescue from the Twilight."  She smiles again, as best she can to comfort you.  "I will come with you, and do my best to help."\par
\cf1 \par
ask gale about flower\par
\cf2 "The music they produce warms my heart... Love is their sunshine," Gale replies, beaming.  "I have a special one you can have," she offers, retrieving a white poppy growing under one of the trees.  "It's not a musical one, but please take this as a token of my friendship."\par
